  "minimum_isolated_validation": [
    "Define a new opt-in capability for independently complete bounded ABC sentence records. Retain all three fields, four emotion values, empty action, duplicate-key rejection and text bounds. Current one-object JSON schema is not NDJSON framing.",
    "Transport owns original Owner/generation, monotonic sequence and terminal success/error frame. Model content cannot supply authority. Never send incomplete JSON, thinking or filler to speech.",
    "First public model-only comparison: first fully valid record, full completion, token count, semantic/schema failures, original deadline. Same model/layers/context/sampling/persona rules. No TTS, Store or playback. No implementation or execution supplied in this report.",
    "Only if meaningful first-record gain appears, test bounded concurrent LLM/TTS under existing GPU admission. Measure first PCM and continuity; record timing alone is insufficient.",
    "Add explicit board-owned unsealed staging that authorizes all original sources and rechecks scope/forget/correction around record/audio acceptance. Final seal creates one whole generated reply and binds complete PCM token/hash/samples. A reviewed append-and-seal Store API is an alternative, not present functionality.",
    "Retain one final PlaybackPlan, owner/generation/cancellation and complete playback ACK. Network end is not speaker completion. Only matching full ACK commits assistant_played; failed, revoked, stale or truncated turns remain incomplete."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "An early spoken sentence cannot be retracted after later correction/failure; stop further audio and retain incomplete status.",
    "Repeated record fields add tokens, limiting short single-sentence benefits.",
    "GPU overlap may worsen audio supply or total generation time.",
    "Bound record bytes/count/characters/sequence/deadline and parse UTF-8/escapes strictly.",
    "Never retry and replay the whole answer after any part was spoken."
  ],
